From d8366188e51c02be5d5995f9d2daaf6430ca1c41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hipac1 <hipac1@lsalab.cs.nthu.edu.tw>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 18:32:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Queue the per-stage kernels and scalar updates async on
 NVHPC, on the synchronous stream

Every RK stage launched 44-68 kernels (by rank) and ~45 scalar host-to-device updates, each followed by a
host synchronization: ~1 ms of GPU idle per stage, which does not shrink with the rank count and
was ~20 % of a stage at 4 GPUs.

On NVHPC, run the default async queue on the synchronous stream (acc_set_cuda_stream at start-up)
and launch the WENO, Riemann-state/HLLC, flux-difference, conversion, boundary, halo pack/unpack
and RK-update kernels and their scalar updates with GPU_ASYNC. Stream order keeps them ordered
with all synchronous GPU work, so the host only waits before device buffers go to MPI. Other
compilers and the OpenMP path are unchanged (GPU_ASYNC is None).

(precheck: format/spell/source-lint/docs pass; toolchain lint fails only on
test_format_tar_zst, a missing zstd on this machine.)
